# ScriptureEarth — Cloudflare Pages _redirects  (ticket 08: legacy URL redirect map)
# Slug strategy (B): the detail slug IS the legacy vanity string <iso>[-<rod>][-<var>],
# so ~3,779 legacy per-entry Redirect 301 lines collapse to 3 placeholder rules.
# Query-string deep links (?iso=/?name=/?idx=/?sortby=country&name=) can't be matched
# here (_redirects is path-only) — they are handled by functions/_middleware.js.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# L1  HTTP->HTTPS and www->apex are NOT expressible reliably in _redirects.
#     Handle at the CF edge:  SSL/TLS -> "Always Use HTTPS" ON, plus one
#     Redirect Rule / Bulk Redirect  www.scriptureearth.org/* -> apex (301).
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
#
# === Precedence guards (MUST come before the /:iso vanity catch-all) =========
# _redirects placeholders are NOT anchored regex; a bare /:iso matches ANY single
# path segment — including top-level asset files and the real section dirs. These
# exact/splat rules match first (first match wins) so /:iso can never shadow them.
# NOTE for build team: any NEW top-level dotted asset added to public/ must get a
# guard line here, OR move the bare /:iso rule into the Function (see REDIRECTS.md).

# Real top-level routes (serve in place, 200 = rewrite-to-self, stops matching)
/browse            /browse/                  301
/browse/*          /browse/:splat            200
/country/*         /country/:splat           200
/language/*        /language/:splat          200
/i18n/*            /i18n/:splat              200
/pagefind/*        /pagefind/:splat          200

# Known top-level static assets (contain '.'/'-', would otherwise be eaten by /:iso)
/favicon.ico       /favicon.ico              200
/site.css          /site.css                 200
/i18n.js           /i18n.js                  200
/search-index.json /search-index.json        200
/sil-logo.webp     /sil-logo.webp            200

# === L3/L4/L5  Locale homepages + localized alias index files -> / + ?lang= ==
# Plain (no query) hits only; deep-link queries on these paths are caught by the
# Function first. Target is "/" pending ticket-04 landing decision (flip to
# /browse/ is a one-line change). /index.php stays 302 while landing is provisional.
/index.php                  /                 302
/00eng.php                  /?lang=eng        301
/00spa.php                  /?lang=spa        301
/00por.php                  /?lang=por        301
/00fra.php                  /?lang=fra        301
/00nld.php                  /?lang=nld        301
/00deu.php                  /?lang=deu        301
/00cmn.php                  /?lang=cmn        301
/00kor.php                  /?lang=kor        301
/00rus.php                  /?lang=rus        301
/00arb.php                  /?lang=arb        301
/00e-Escrituras_Indice.php  /?lang=spa        301
/00d-Bijbel_Indice.php      /?lang=nld        301
/00de-Sprachindex.php       /?lang=deu        301
/00f-Ecritures_Indice.php   /?lang=fra        301
/00i-Scripture_Index.php    /?lang=eng        301
/00p-Escrituras_Indice.php  /?lang=por        301

# === L2  Vanity short URLs -> language detail (3,779 legacy rows in 3 rules) ==
# Most-specific first (2 dashes, then 1, then 0). The slug equals the old vanity
# string, so this is an exact 1:1 mapping with no lookup. e.g.
#   /acr-00000-a -> /language/acr-00000-a/   (34 legacy rows)
#   /abt-3053    -> /language/abt-3053/       (175 legacy rows)
#   /aaa         -> /language/aaa/            (3,570 legacy rows)
/:iso-:rod-:var    /language/:iso-:rod-:var/  301
/:iso-:rod         /language/:iso-:rod/       301
/:iso              /language/:iso/            301
